# loop-bash-repeat-poll: RED→GREEN reproduction fixture for the loop-repeat guard v1.2
# (task loop-repeat-guard, IDEAS §8).
#
# Scenario: a worker burns identical bash polling calls — `cat root.jsonl | tail -1` —
# mimicking the 2026-10-12 incident (`p9-dossier-runtime-debug2` polled every ~2m45s for hours).
# Each turn's bash RESULT carries a fresh timestamp/counter (the incident's `tail` printed a
# new mail timestamp every iteration) — so the detector MUST fire on identical ARGS with
# DIFFERENT outputs. v1.2 revision (commit 4a2cc39) drops result-hash from the fingerprint
# precisely because result-hash would defeat the detector on its own motivating case.
#
# NOTE: the fixture uses `cat root.jsonl | tail -1` (instant return) instead of the incident's
# `sleep 165; tail -1 root.jsonl` because the mock-llm lane cannot sleep for 165s per turn.
# The detector's fingerprint is `hash(toolName + normalizedArgs)` — the command string is
# what matters, not the sleep duration. The lane command sets PI_SWARM_LOOP_REPEAT_WINDOW_MS=0
# to disable the time-span gate deterministically (fixtures never set env).
#
# Shape (24 turns; pacing keeps the active segment open — toolUse stops keep the run looping
# tool->tool without settling mid-block, so segment time accrues from scripted delayMs):
#   t1..t5:   5 identical bash polls (milestone k=1 boundary at call 5)
#   t6..t10:  5 more identical bash polls (milestone k=2 boundary at call 10)
#   t11..t15: 5 more identical bash polls (milestone k=3 boundary at call 15)
#   t16..t20: 5 more identical bash polls (milestone-4 boundary at call 20 → root escalation)
#   t21..t23: 3 post-escalation polls (persisted latch: no re-escalation, no 4th continuation)
#   t24:      terminal stop
# Every delayMs is 15–25ms; all tool names are lowercase pi-builtin (bash). The bash RESULT
# text varies per turn (fresh timestamp) — the detector must NOT use result-hash.
#
# Expected GREEN (detector landed): mid-run self-nudge after the 5th bash (milestone k=1),
# 10th (k=2), 15th (k=3) — each nudge text (LOOP-REPEAT marker family, milestone number,
# call count, span) lands in the NEXT model request via turn_end custom_message + continue:true.
# Exactly 3 mid-run continuations; final turn stop. Root escalation fires ONCE at milestone-4.
# Expected RED (pre-code reproduction): transcript shows NO nudge text anywhere, zero extra
# requests — the run burns all 20+ bash polls silently.
{"name": "bash poll 1/20", "stopReason": "toolUse", "events": [{"type": "text", "delayMs": 20, "text": "Polling root for reply.", "chunks": ["Polling root ", "for reply."]}, {"type": "toolcall", "delayMs": 20, "name": "bash", "id": "p-1", "arguments": {"command": "cat root.jsonl | tail -1"}}]}
